1. The original ask was to rename the type RestoreMode to RecoveryClaimMode everywhere in this file (imports, variables, API calls, defaults), but the code still uses RestoreMode throughout.  
2. Needed changes include (but are not limited to) the following:  
   - Line 24:  
     ```java
     // old
     import org.apache.flink.core.execution.RestoreMode;
     // should be
     import org.apache.flink.core.execution.RecoveryClaimMode;
     ```  
   - Lines 700–701:  
     ```java
     // old
     final RestoreMode restoreMode;
     // should be
     final RecoveryClaimMode claimMode;
     ```  
   - Lines 702–706 and 707–711: change both calls to ConfigurationUtils.convertValue to use RecoveryClaimMode.class instead of RestoreMode.class.  
   - Line 715: use the new default option, e.g. StateRecoveryOptions.CLAIM_MODE.defaultValue(), not StateRecoveryOptions.RESTORE_MODE.defaultValue().  
   - Also adjust the variable passed into SavepointRestoreSettings.forPath(...) to match the renamed type.  

Because these renames haven’t been applied, the task is INCOMPLETE.
